# LLMHub on NCSA DeltaAI (GH200, aarch64 compute) — what differs from Delta.
# COMMITTED. Sourced by delta.env when LLMHUB_CLUSTER=deltaai, BEFORE its
# defaults, so every value here wins and every value NOT here is Delta's
# default and is correct for DeltaAI as well. Same `${VAR:-…}` form, so an
# export or a stack's local.env still overrides.
#
# Values were measured 2026-09-17..21; the evidence is in llm-service-software
# (knowledge-base/llmhub-deltaai.md, knowledge-base/llmhub-deltaai-vllm-image.md).

# ------------------------------------------------ roots on the shared /projects
# /projects is the only filesystem Delta and DeltaAI share, and svcdeltallmhub
# is the SAME account (uid 91544) on both, so a root keyed on profile or $USER
# alone collides unconditionally (GAP-013). Everything DeltaAI keeps there sits
# under a `deltaai` name. Delta's roots are left exactly where they were, so no
# Delta stack moves — in particular Delta's dev secrets.env, the only copy of
# its CILogon credentials, stays put.
#
#   deploy root   Delta /projects/bfmz/<user>/llmhub-<profile>
#                 here  /projects/bfmz/<user>/llmhub-deltaai-<profile>
#   job workspaces Delta /projects/llmhub/<profile>
#                 here  /projects/llmhub/deltaai/<profile>
#   vec-inf logs  Delta /projects/llmhub          (masked in impersonate mode —
#                 here  /projects/llmhub/deltaai   the backend sets log_dir per user)
LLMHUB_BASE="${LLMHUB_BASE:-/projects/bfmz/${USER}}"
LLMHUB_DEPLOY_ROOT="${LLMHUB_DEPLOY_ROOT:-${LLMHUB_BASE}/llmhub-deltaai-${LLMHUB_PROFILE}}"
LLMHUB_SHARED_WORK_ROOT="${LLMHUB_SHARED_WORK_ROOT:-/projects/llmhub/deltaai/${LLMHUB_PROFILE}}"
LLMHUB_VEC_INF_LOG_DIR="${LLMHUB_VEC_INF_LOG_DIR:-/projects/llmhub/deltaai}"

# The torch-inductor cache is WRITTEN by vLLM's compile step, and one directory
# would otherwise hold x86_64/A100 and aarch64/GH200 artifacts side by side.
# vLLM keys them by configuration so sharing is probably safe, but it has never
# been tested and a wrong-kernel hit would not look like a cache bug. A second
# directory costs only disk. Service user only, exactly like Delta's: anyone
# else gets a per-stack cache under the deploy root (delta.env). The backend
# derives the directories it grants svcllmhub* ACLs on from the rendered bind,
# so nothing else has to know about this path.
if [ "$USER" = "${LLMHUB_SERVICE_USER:-svcdeltallmhub}" ]; then
    LLMHUB_TORCH_CACHE="${LLMHUB_TORCH_CACHE:-/projects/modelcache/public/torch_inductor-deltaai}"
fi
# The Hugging Face weights ARE shared: architecture-neutral, 43 G, and on
# /projects/modelcache, which counts against no quota. delta.env's default stands.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ slurm / vec-inf
LLMHUB_SLURM_ACCOUNT="${LLMHUB_SLURM_ACCOUNT:-bfmz-dtai-gh}"
# MaxNodes=2, MaxTime=02:00:00, and QOS qos_ghx4int caps each user at ONE
# running job — so each svcllmhub<netid> can serve one model at a time. Right
# for dev; revisit (ghx4: 2 days, no per-user cap) before production.
LLMHUB_LAUNCH_PARTITION="${LLMHUB_LAUNCH_PARTITION:-ghx4-interactive}"
# Node GRES is gpu:nvidia_gh200_120gb:4; vec-inf emits gpu:<type>:<n>, and
# `sbatch --test-only --gres=gpu:nvidia_gh200_120gb:4` is accepted. It is not in
# the environment.yaml allowed_values list, which is advisory — the field is
# Union[Literal[...], str], verified to accept it.
LLMHUB_LAUNCH_RESOURCE_TYPE="${LLMHUB_LAUNCH_RESOURCE_TYPE:-nvidia_gh200_120gb}"
# Consumed by srun on the HOST side, so it cannot live in the image (which runs
# --containall). Not required for the fabric to work — gate job 3188139 selected
# CXI on all 8 ranks without it — but HPE calls disable_rdzv_get required for the
# FI_CXI_RX_MATCH_MODE=hybrid the image sets, and the only at-scale validation
# of that tuning had it set. The VM has no DeltaAI Lmod modules, so this is the
# only place it can come from.
LLMHUB_CONTAINER_LOAD_CMD="${LLMHUB_CONTAINER_LOAD_CMD:-export SLURM_NETWORK=single_node_vni,disable_rdzv_get}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- inference
# DeltaAI cannot run Delta's v0.19.1: its libfabric.so.1 and libcxi.so.1 need
# GLIBC_2.38, and every arm64 vllm-openai tag before v0.28.0 is Ubuntu 22.04 /
# glibc 2.35. Recipe: devops/apptainers/deltaai/. Built and gated 2026-09-17
# (build 3167290, gate 3168241 — CXI selected on all 8 ranks), promoted
# 2026-09-21, sha256 4395a0c67b8fc3752d9571c898456820e9bdfc7feb21d075332be1f71497146c.
# production keeps delta.env's /sw/llmhub/vllm.sif, which resolves against
# DeltaAI's own /sw and does not exist until an image is promoted to it.
LLMHUB_VLLM_SIF_DEV="${LLMHUB_VLLM_SIF_DEV:-/sw/llmhub/vllm-v0.28.0-slingshot-deltaai.sif}"

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- host
# require_operator() compares `hostname -s` against this. RHEL 9.6 x86_64, the
# same VM template as Delta's; mounts DeltaAI's /sw and /u; ClusterName delta-gh.
LLMHUB_VM_HOST="${LLMHUB_VM_HOST:-dtai-svc-llmaas01.delta.ncsa.illinois.edu}"
